From 8e49a9ce08613195f1a89cd5212b8e0cf289aa57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alex <alex.decious@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:07:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] linux: left click on the tray opens the window

libappindicator's tray item has no Activate method, so StatusNotifierItem
hosts cannot report a left click, and Handy only handles one on Windows.
Tauri 2.12 depends on tray-icon 0.25, whose KSNI backend turns Activate
into a left click event. Enable it on Linux and use the Windows handler
there too; right click still opens the menu.

Bumps tauri to 2.12.4 and @tauri-apps/api to match (tauri-cli refuses a
minor-version mismatch). Drops the tao fork pin: tao 0.37.1, which tauri
2.12 uses, contains tao #1218 and #1274.
